.TITLE "netstat"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Displays active TCP connections, ports on which the computer is listening, Ethernet statistics, and the IP routing table. It is an essential tool for __network monitoring__.

.DIV "ALIAS"

.DIV "TLDR"
**netstat**
Displays active TCP connections for the local machine.
> 

**netstat -a**
Displays all active TCP connections and the TCP and UDP ports on which the computer is listening.
> __-a__ all flag

**netstat -n**
Displays active TCP connections but shows addresses and port numbers in numerical form.
> __-n__ numerical flag

**netstat -o**
Displays active TCP connections and includes the process ID (PID) for each connection.
> __-o__ owner flag

**netstat -e**
Displays Ethernet statistics, such as the number of bytes and packets sent and received.
> __-e__ ethernet flag

**netstat -r**
Displays the contents of the IP routing table.
> __-r__ routing table flag

.DIV "SUMMARY"
Combine flags like __netstat -a -n -o__ to see all active connections with their PIDs in a numerical format. This is particularly useful for identifying which application is using a specific port.

.DIV "SEE ALSO"
**windows:ipconfig** **windows:tracert**

documentation: __https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows-server/administration/windows-commands/netstat__
